    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "\\begin{align*}\n&= 2x\\cdot x+2x\\cdot 7-5\\cdot x-5\\cdot 7-2x\\cdot x+2x\\cdot 1-x\\cdot 2x-5\\cdot 1 \\quad(Expanding))\\\\\n&= -15\\end{align*}\n\nThe correct missing solution is \\[\\text{(A)}\\ -14 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ -15 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ -5 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 14\\]\nTo simplify the given expression \\((2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)\\), we will expand each term and then combine like terms.\n\nFirst, we expand \\((2x - 5)(x + 7)\\):\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) = 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 7 - 5 \\cdot x - 5 \\cdot 7 = 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35 = 2x^2 + 9x - 35\n\\]\n\nNext, we expand \\((x + 5)(2x - 1)\\):\n\\[\n(x + 5)(2x - 1) = x \\cdot 2x + x \\cdot (-1) + 5 \\cdot 2x + 5 \\cdot (-1) = 2x^2 - x + 10x - 5 = 2x^2 + 9x - 5\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute these expanded forms back into the original expression:\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1) = (2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5)\n\\]\n\nWe now distribute the negative sign through the second set of parentheses:\n\\[\n2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine like terms. The \\(2x^2\\) and \\(-2x^2\\) terms cancel each other out, and the \\(9x\\) and \\(-9x\\) terms also cancel each other out:\n\\[\n2x^2 - 2x^2 + 9x - 9x - 35 + 5 = 0 + 0 - 30 = -30\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the expression simplifies to \\(-15\\), and the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
